WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.980
To speak well you have to speak a lot and
you have to speak in intensive situations.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:10.680
Hi, Steve Kaufmann here and today I
want to talk about what is really, you

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:16.320
know, the fourth goal in my hierarchy
of goals, uh, in language learning

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.420
and that speaking, uh, remember if you
enjoy these videos, please subscribe,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.280
click on the bell for notifications.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:27.930
And uh, if you follow me on a podcast
service, please leave a comment.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:28.730
I do appreciate it.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.535
So for many people,
speaking is the first goal.

00:00:32.805 --> 00:00:33.465
I want to speak.

00:00:35.115 --> 00:00:39.915
If you have followed me here, you
know that I have the view that is

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.405
not realistic to speak from day one.

00:00:42.405 --> 00:00:47.865
Let's say if you're a, if you're in a
situation, like my situation, when I was

00:00:47.865 --> 00:00:53.535
in Japan, where I'm surrounded by the
language, I can try to speak to people.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.220
Uh, but it won't be my major activity
initially, because I don't have the words.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.210
If you go back to my hierarchy
of goals, I don't have the words.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.710
I haven't read these words.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.560
I haven't listened to enough of the
language so that I can understand.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.940
I don't have the listening comprehension.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.960
So my ability to talk to
people is very limited.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.730
So I am not that keen under
normal circumstances to start

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.370
talking, I find it frustrating.

00:01:21.945 --> 00:01:22.965
Almost intimidating.

00:01:22.965 --> 00:01:25.664
If I don't understand what people
are saying, I'm not so keen to

00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:26.895
engage them in conversation.

00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:28.485
So what are my goals?

00:01:28.935 --> 00:01:34.245
My goal, I tend to say, you know, I
used to wait until I had about 10,000

00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:38.535
words in language before I would start
speaking to, say, a tutor online.

00:01:39.525 --> 00:01:45.285
Uh, now I've dropped that to about
three to 5,000 words, uh, because

00:01:45.285 --> 00:01:48.705
I, uh, maybe I've become better
at learning these languages.

00:01:49.215 --> 00:01:50.855
And so I don't mind the struggle.

00:01:51.975 --> 00:01:55.395
Um, less, uh, self-conscious
about not understanding.

00:01:55.845 --> 00:01:59.744
And in any case, when I start
with a tutor, I'll typically get

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:00.884
on there once or twice a week.

00:02:01.035 --> 00:02:04.664
So that's not a major investment of
time because where I want to continue

00:02:04.664 --> 00:02:08.984
to invest my time is listening
and reading, acquiring words.

00:02:09.794 --> 00:02:15.285
However, I do recognize that to speak
well, and we all want to speak well,

00:02:15.555 --> 00:02:19.685
we all want to speak well, um, to
speak while you have to speak a lot.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.220
And you have to speak
in intensive situations.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.360
So to have a short
conversation, because you're...

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.890
you go to someone in Chinatown and use a
few words of Chinese, or you order your,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.940
you know, whatever dish in a Chinese
restaurant in Chinese, to me, that's not a

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.540
very intense engagement with the language.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.070
On the other hand, if you are with people
and you're speaking Chinese and you're

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.190
with them over dinner and everybody's
speaking Chinese, and you're speaking

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.065
Chinese and you're participating in the
conference, that's tremendously powerful.

00:02:52.364 --> 00:02:56.535
That's first of all input, that
is high resonance input because

00:02:56.535 --> 00:02:57.885
you're in that conversation.

00:02:57.885 --> 00:03:00.855
It's real and you're struggling
to get your meaning out.

00:03:01.245 --> 00:03:04.245
And there's a lot of pressure
because everyone is speaking

00:03:04.245 --> 00:03:05.325
very quickly in Chinese.

00:03:05.325 --> 00:03:09.885
And when you go to speak you feel you
don't have the time to say what you want

00:03:09.885 --> 00:03:12.315
to say, those are all great situations.

00:03:12.704 --> 00:03:17.280
But to be in that situation, you have
to have a certain level of preparation.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.990
So that's why I put so much emphasis
on acquiring words, reading to

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:25.560
reinforce those words, listening to
improve your listening comprehension.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:32.040
And then when you get the opportunity,
try to put yourself in intense situations.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.300
And when you're in that intense
situation, just go for it.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.460
And, you know, if you struggle to say
what you want to say, if you feel that

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.720
you you're slowing down the conversation
for everyone else, because that...

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.980
you know, going to be impatient, but
mostly they're not going to be impatient.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.710
They're willing to wait for you
to say what you want to say.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:58.170
So I think it's very important if,
if we have built up our confidence in

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:02.670
the language and our comprehension,
if we have words, we may search for

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:06.300
the words, but somewhere we know we
have some of the words we want to use.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:12.000
If you have that level of preparation,
you can get into higher intensity

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.370
conversation opportunities.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.660
It's a bit like when I exercise now,
I'm doing these kettle bell workouts,

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.060
high intensity interval training.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:25.530
There's something to be said for high
intensity, to be in a high intensive

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.860
high intensity, uh, language situation.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.500
You have to be prepared for it.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:39.510
Uh, just to sit like, uh, and talk
about the weather, uh, with five or

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:45.165
six other students, it's not that it's
not effective, but I think spending

00:04:45.165 --> 00:04:49.395
that time with the language, doing a
lot of listening and reading and, and,

00:04:49.395 --> 00:04:53.715
and working on acquiring more words is
a more useful way to spend your time.

00:04:54.315 --> 00:04:58.365
And you can save that speaking
opportunity, whether one-on-one

00:04:58.365 --> 00:05:03.945
or in a group, till you
have sufficient a sufficient

00:05:03.945 --> 00:05:08.035
vocabulary, sufficient confidence,
sufficient listening confidence.

00:05:08.445 --> 00:05:11.925
So that you can actually have a very
intense even an hour one-on-one.

00:05:11.925 --> 00:05:17.445
Now, when I speak with my Persian tutor,
Sahra, we cover a lot of ground and

00:05:17.445 --> 00:05:21.435
there's a lot of words that I can't
remember, and she has to remind me, but

00:05:22.544 --> 00:05:29.100
then I get from her my conversation report
on LingQ where she has 15 or so words and

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.640
phrases that I didn't use correctly or
where I struggled or I'd forgotten them.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:38.130
And, uh, and she records this and
I listen to it and I may forget

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.270
it again for the next time.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:44.370
And in fact, I can see in my record of my
conversation, reports going back, say six

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.780
months that I make the same mistakes every
week to a large extent, but gradually,

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.600
gradually, gradually I get better.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:56.865
And so the, um, if I'm initially
maybe only talking twice a week, I may

00:05:56.865 --> 00:06:01.035
eventually step that up, particularly
if I have an opportunity to go to

00:06:01.035 --> 00:06:05.145
the country, because when you go
to the country, your opportunity to

00:06:05.145 --> 00:06:06.705
speak is going to be much greater.

00:06:07.155 --> 00:06:11.325
And I like to prepare myself as much as
possible before going to the country.

00:06:11.595 --> 00:06:17.085
So when I went to Greece or to Romania,
then I would beforehand step up the number

00:06:17.085 --> 00:06:21.930
of conversations with my tutor to maybe
four times a week, five times a week.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:28.050
And then when I arrive in the country,
when I was on Crete, I have a chance.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.870
I have a chance of understanding
what they're saying.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.930
I have a chance that I can say
what I want to say, and they won't

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.800
come back at me, come back at me in
English, because if you don't have

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.050
that level, then you may miss...

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.020
you may not take full advantage
of the opportunity of being in the

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.950
country because the locals who don't
necessarily want to be your teacher,

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.430
they just want to communicate if they
sense that you can't understand and you

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.659
can't communicate, they'll switch to
a language where it's easier for them

00:06:54.659 --> 00:06:56.130
to communicate, which may be English.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:07:01.440
So I think it's very important to
take full advantage of that intensive,

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:05.789
you know, speaking opportunity that
visiting the country can represent,

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.830
to prepare for it ahead of time.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:16.845
So to summarize the goal in speaking,
in my view, is to get to a level

00:07:16.845 --> 00:07:19.275
where you can defend yourself.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:20.715
You don't have to be perfect.

00:07:20.715 --> 00:07:24.015
You can have poor pronunciation,
you can forget words, but you

00:07:24.015 --> 00:07:25.275
understand what people are saying.

00:07:25.275 --> 00:07:30.165
You can defend yourself so you can
hang in there, hang in there in these

00:07:30.165 --> 00:07:34.695
more intense, uh, engagements with
people in the language, which are

00:07:34.695 --> 00:07:40.085
going to be very powerful for you to
develop your speaking skills, which...

00:07:40.265 --> 00:07:44.105
while I put it as the fourth goal,
because I know there are three

00:07:44.105 --> 00:07:47.435
other goals that have to come first,
but it is a very important goal.

00:07:47.525 --> 00:07:49.355
We all want to end up speaking well.

00:07:49.715 --> 00:07:51.455
So thank you for listening.

00:07:51.515 --> 00:07:52.565
I hope that was useful.

00:07:53.045 --> 00:07:53.435
Bye for now.

